 kit platform - lists the services, toolchains, tools, and settings kit runs with

   one of
   *kit platform*  lists the services, toolchains, tools, and settings kit runs with

     --text   --json   --jq
                           prints the stages as text, even on a terminal

   --stages      prints the stages, one per line, in order, the same over any workspace
   --marks       prints a mark per stage, as one JSON object, which changes when what the stage
                 draws does: a hash of kit.yml for settings; for toolchains and tools, of the files
                 the toolchains and the dependency providers pin from and of those that keep kit's
                 choice; and for services, of all of those, the clone's git configuration, which
                 holds its remotes, and .kit/policy
   services      {capability, service, provider, chosen, ready}: capability is hosting, review, ci,
                 releases, tracking <prefix>, toolchain, dependencies <provider>, or policy, and
                 dependencies alone where no provider's manifest and lock are here; service is what
                 answers it, as github, mise, or patterns, null for none, as for the forge's with no
                 remote or a ci the forge lacks; provider is kit's module that reaches it, as
                 forge/github; chosen is set where kit.yml or a recorded choice names it, else
                 inferred; ready is whether its tool is there and signed in, null where it has none.
                 A forge or a policy engine kit.yml names wrong is {error}, its line, under errors
   toolchains    {provider, role, usable, active, chosen, fills}, as kit toolchains --json prints
                 them, keyed by provider and role: mise project
   tools         {name, pinned, installed, from}, as kit tools --json prints them, keyed by from and
                 name; ambient, {name, path, from}
   settings      {setting, value, from}: value is kit.yml's, or the schema's default, null where it
                 names none; from is set or default


 kit platform
